{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And not one</b> — of you acted according to law, and his spirit remained to him. And if you say: what does the One seek? Seed of Elohim, through the commandments of HaShem. And the meaning of “and his spirit remained to him” is not to intermingle with a foreign daughter; therefore it is written: “and guard yourselves in your spirit,” and “with the wife of your youth let not your spirit betray.”"], :book :malachi, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The Hebrew conjunctions in the opening line are ambiguous; I have rendered the parsed sense without expanding the compressed syntax."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Malachi -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/malachi"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:15.971889480Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}